# Per-path token CHAIN ceilings, gated by `bbx budget`. itok's format,
# reused rather than reinvented -- a second format for one job would be two
# readings of one rule.
#
# WHAT THIS CEILING IS: the cost of REACHING a node -- root plus every
# ancestor plus itself -- which is what a worker pays before it sees any code.
# Measured on the target tier (gpt-oss:20b, 131,072 window, 28,543 entry cost,
# 102,529 working), the spec share is ~25%, so ~25,000 tokens.
#
# It forces a REVIEW, not a shrink. Set with real slack (~15-30%): a ceiling a
# hair above current turns every legitimate addition into a raise, and a
# threshold raised reflexively trains the reflex instead of catching the
# problem. Raises belong in a commit with their reason.
#
# Measured 2026-08-01, `bbx budget`: root 9,164 · src 9,544 · deepest
# src/tdd 13,137. Ceilings sit ~20% above each.
SPEC.md        11000
src            11500
src/tdd        16000
src/fed        14000
src/ollama     13000
src/plan       13000
src/review     12500
src/lens       12000
